<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francysk Skaryna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1490–c. 1551</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Francisk Skorina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francysk Skaryna was a printer, translator and physician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. In 1517-1519 he printed books of the Bible in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> in a Church Slavonic close to the vernacular, and in the 1520s he set up the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>. He is regarded as a founder of Belarusian printing and literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francysk-skaryna.jpg" alt="Francysk Skaryna" width="320" height="497" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francišak Skaryna · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Franci%C5%A1ak_Skaryna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
